Create a reusable ClusterRole and bind it to a single namespace.

1. Define a Cluster-Wide Role Template

cat <<EOF > cluster-role-view.yaml
apiVersion: rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1
kind: ClusterRole
metadata:
  name: namespace-auditor
rules:
- apiGroups: [""]
  resources: ["configmaps", "services", "endpoints"]
  verbs: ["get", "list", "watch"]
EOF

kubectl apply -f cluster-role-view.yaml


2. Bind It Locally via RoleBinding
Even though namespace-auditor is a ClusterRole, attaching it with a RoleBinding restricts 
its permissions strictly to the default namespace:

kubectl create rolebinding runner-auditor-binding \
  --clusterrole=namespace-auditor \
  --serviceaccount=default:github-runner-sa \
  --namespace=default


  3. Verify the Namespace Boundary

# Permitted in default namespace:
kubectl auth can-i list configmaps --namespace=default --as=system:serviceaccount:default:github-runner-sa

# Forbidden in kube-system namespace:
kubectl auth can-i list configmaps --namespace=kube-system --as=system:serviceaccount:default:github-runner-sa

The first query will return yes, and the second will return no.

